==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Crazed Whale Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Manic Island Cat''' when obtained from [[Ogre Island (Deadly)|Fish Maniac]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Crazed Fish Cat can be considered one of the most cost-effective units in the game, and one of the strongest [[:Category:Crazed Cats|Crazed Cats]] due to its fortified health and attack power. With its low cost, it can be considered a very good anti-Red unit and general unit alike, further augmented in its true form.

While it does have the ability to perform highly damaging Critical Hits which can cripple if not instantly kill many metals, the chance is too low to make it a reliable anti-metal but it can be brought on mixed stages.
Crazed Fish is also extremely useful on Into the Future's [[Moon (Into the Future)|Moon]] in Chapter 1, allowing players to get timed score rewards on their first try.

When boosted by Strong Effect Up [[Cat Combo]]s, this and normal [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]]'s stats become similar to that of some anti-red ubers. This effect is most notable on stages like [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|Realm of Carnage]], where being in possession of these combos make a huge difference due to certain interactions.

===True Form===
Manic Island Cat gains no new abilities, but instead gains a boost to its health and damage. The boosts turn Manic Island into one of the best free units obtainable, as it is now an extremely powerful general tank. Manic Island has 6K DPS and 44K health at level 30, which is ridiculous for its low cost of 735–nearly half that of Island Cat while retaining higher stats. Combined with its acceptable 8s cooldown, Manic Island can be spammed to absorb large amounts of damage and deal high amounts of damage over time.

However, this is not all. Manic Island's stats go crazy against Reds with its Strong Against, having '''110K health and 11K DPS''' at level 30, assuming all [[Fruit Treasures]] are active. Combined with its shockingly low cost for its stats and its higher speed as compared to Normal Island, Manic Island can absolutely dominate Red-focused stages like [[Color of Blood (Merciless)|Color of Blood]] and [[Red Alert]] as well as decimating Red Enemies like [[Berserkory]] and [[Professor A.]]. Manic Island is an excellent unit to throw in if you have an open slot, and can be used on almost every stage in the game, with its sheer cost efficiency outweighing many of its weaknesses.

Overall, Manic Island is an extremely potent general unit and has a true form definitely worth beating [[Ogre Island (Deadly)|its awakening stage]].

